  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, PCA, singleprofile) achieves 0.485 accuracy, establishing RNA as the dominant modality, while config_010 (image-only, ResNet50) is very weak at 0.208, suggesting image contributes little signal on its own. This makes the RNA representation quality the most critical design decision for any future multimodal experiment. Question tested: Does a learned nonlinear RNA encoder (scvi_n200) outperform the simple linear PCA (pca_n2000) baseline? This is a clean single-variable change from config_001, isolating the encoder choice. Why this is the best next experiment: The RNA encoder underpins every downstream multimodal configuration (configs 016–051). If scvi_n200 substantially improves on 0.485, it justifies investing in learned encoders for multimodal fusion; if it does not, PCA is sufficient and we should focus budget on profile/aggregation/fusion choices instead. This experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most impactful design axis before committing budget to more complex multimodal or multiprofile configurations."
}

